window.AKI_SEARCH=[{"u": "install.html", "t": "Install", "h": "", "x": "One command builds aki and tells you what to sign in to. curl -fsSL https://nathan-poncet.github.io/aki/install.sh | sh The script builds aki from its repository with Cargo and installs one program, aki , in ~/.cargo/bin . It then tells you whether glab and gh are present. It installs nothing else and needs no administrator rights."}, {"u": "install.html#requirements", "t": "Install", "h": "Requirements", "x": "macOS or Linux. The Rust toolchain ( cargo ). Without it the script stops and says so; AKI_RUSTUP=1 lets it install the toolchain with rustup first. git . For GitLab, the glab CLI; for GitHub, the gh CLI. aki uses their logins. A token in an environment variable works too: see Sources ."}, {"u": "install.html#other-ways", "t": "Install", "h": "Other ways", "x": "cargo install --locked --git https://github.com/nathan-poncet/aki git clone https://github.com/nathan-poncet/aki cd aki cargo install --path . curl -fsSL https://nathan-poncet.github.io/aki/install.sh | AKI_REF=main sh AKI_REF is a tag, a branch or a commit."}, {"u": "install.html#sign-in", "t": "Install", "h": "Sign in", "x": "aki reads each service with the login of its own CLI. Sign in to the ones you use: glab auth login or gh auth login Jira needs three lines of configuration: see Sources ."}, {"u": "install.html#check", "t": "Install", "h": "Check", "x": "aki doctor It prints one line per source: who you are signed in as, or why the source cannot be read."}, {"u": "install.html#update", "t": "Install", "h": "Update", "x": "Run the install command again. Cargo rebuilds only when the sources changed."}, {"u": "install.html#uninstall", "t": "Install", "h": "Uninstall", "x": "cargo uninstall aki rm -rf ~/.config/aki ~/.cache/aki ~/.local/state/aki The second line removes your configuration and spaces, the cache, and what you set aside."}, {"u": "quick-start.html", "t": "Quick start", "h": "", "x": "From an installed aki to a board you can read, in five steps."}, {"u": "quick-start.html#1-check-the-sources", "t": "Quick start", "h": "1. Check the sources", "x": "aki doctor output ✓ gitlab signed in as nat ✓ github signed in as nat With no configuration, aki uses gitlab.com when glab is installed and github.com when gh is. A source marked ✗ says why: usually a missing glab auth login or gh auth login ."}, {"u": "quick-start.html#2-open-the-board", "t": "Quick start", "h": "2. Open the board", "x": "aki Two panes: To do , what waits on you, and Waiting , what you cannot move further. The board refreshes every 30 seconds and shows the last known state while the first reading is under way."}, {"u": "quick-start.html#3-read-a-line", "t": "Quick start", "h": "3. Read a line", "x": "one task ▲ Re-review api!889 Typed errors for the key store @ana +1 130 5d Part Meaning ▲ ▴ Hot, warm: the urgency score passed a threshold. Re-review The most pressing reason the task is listed. Yellow: yours to do. Cyan: waits on others. api!889 The repository and the reference. @ana Who is on the other side: the author when you review. +1 One more reason than the one shown. 130 The urgency score, in panes ordered by urgency. 5d For how long the most pressing reason has been true."}, {"u": "quick-start.html#4-five-keys", "t": "Quick start", "h": "4. Five keys", "x": "Key Does ↑ ↓ ← → Move between tasks and panes. Enter Open the task in the browser, on the thread when there is one. i Explain the task: why it is listed and how its score adds up. p Set it aside until a day, or until it moves. ? Every key. The full list is on Keys ."}, {"u": "quick-start.html#5-make-it-yours", "t": "Quick start", "h": "5. Make it yours", "x": "aki config init This writes ~/.config/aki/config.toml with every setting at its default and a comment on each. Common first changes: Add Jira . Keep your drafts in a pane of their own . Split work and personal into spaces . Choose the agent that a opens ."}, {"u": "quick-start.html#without-the-board", "t": "Quick start", "h": "Without the board", "x": "aki list --todo aki list --count aki list --json aki list prints the board once. --count gives one line for a prompt or a status bar; --json is for scripts. See Command line ."}, {"u": "rules.html", "t": "Rules", "h": "", "x": "Every reason a task is on the board is a rule. Each rule can be turned off, moved to the other side, or reordered. For each merge request, pull request and ticket you are involved in, aki looks at who spoke last in every thread, the state of reviews and approvals, the pipeline, the branch, and the ticket's status. Each fact that asks something of someone becomes a reason . A task is listed once, under its most pressing reason; the others show in the detail pane."}, {"u": "rules.html#to-do", "t": "Rules", "h": "To do", "x": "The next step is yours. Label Rule Priority When Review review_requested 10 Your review is requested and you have not started. Re-review re_review 20 You reviewed, and since then something moved (see Re-reviews ). Reply reply_needed 30 Someone waits for your answer in a thread, or mentioned you. Mentioned ticket_mentioned 35 Someone mentioned you on a ticket and you have not commented since. Resolve threads thread_to_resolve 40 A thread you opened was answered: check it and close it. Fix checks checks_failed 50 The pipeline of your change failed. Fix conflicts conflicts 55 Your change conflicts with its target branch. Rebase rebase 57 Your change is behind its target branch. Not shown when it already conflicts. Merge ready_to_merge 60 Your change is approved, green, with no open thread, and you can merge it. Assigned assigned 65 A change you neither wrote nor review is assigned to you. Ask a review no_reviewer 70 Your change is ready and nobody was asked to review it. In progress ticket_in_progress 75 A ticket of yours is in progress. To do ticket_todo 80 A ticket of yours is not started. Nudge nudge 85 A waiting item has not moved for a number of days (off by default, see Nudge ). Finish draft draft_to_finish 90 Your change is still a draft."}, {"u": "rules.html#waiting", "t": "Rules", "h": "Waiting", "x": "You cannot move it further: someone or something else has the next step. Label Rule Priority When Awaiting review awaiting_review 10 Your change waits for reviewers. The detail names who has not looked. Awaiting author awaiting_author 20 You reviewed; nothing new since. Awaiting reply awaiting_reply 30 You answered; the other side has to close the thread. Checks running checks_running 40 The pipeline of your change is running. Blocked ticket_blocked 50 A ticket of yours is blocked by another, or in a waiting status. Draft draft_by_other 60 A change you review is still a draft. One reason to do is enough to put the whole task in To do ."}, {"u": "rules.html#change-a-rule", "t": "Rules", "h": "Change a rule", "x": "Any rule takes three settings. A lower priority comes first. ~/.config/aki/config.toml [rules.draft_to_finish] enabled = false [rules.checks_running] bucket = \"todo\" priority = 45 aki rules prints every rule as it applies. An unknown rule name is an error, so a typo never silently disables a rule."}, {"u": "rules.html#threads", "t": "Rules", "h": "Threads", "x": "Teams differ on who closes a review thread once it is answered. [threads] who_resolves = \"reviewer\" ignore_bots = true Value Effect \"reviewer\" Whoever opened the thread checks the answer and resolves it. An answered thread you opened is Resolve threads ; one you answered is Awaiting reply . \"author\" The author resolves threads once addressed. \"anyone\" No convention: only who spoke last counts. With ignore_bots , a bot's comment never gives anyone the next step."}, {"u": "rules.html#re-reviews", "t": "Rules", "h": "Re-reviews", "x": "After your first review, any of these triggers makes a re-review due: [re_review] triggers = [\"author_replied\", \"new_commits\", \"re_requested\", \"approval_reset\"] after_approval = false Trigger Fires when author_replied Someone answered in a thread you take part in. new_commits Commits were pushed after your last review activity. re_requested Your review was requested again. approval_reset Your approval was reset or dismissed. all_threads_answered Every thread you opened has been answered or resolved. Not in the default list. after_approval = true lets a re-review be due on a change you already approved."}, {"u": "rules.html#drafts", "t": "Rules", "h": "Drafts", "x": "[drafts] mine = \"todo\" others = \"wait\" Setting Value Effect mine \"todo\" Your drafts are listed with everything else that waits on you. \"apart\" They stay on the board but leave To do , the counts and the notifications. They show only in panes filtered on is:draft . \"ignore\" They are left off the board until they are ready. others \"wait\" A draft you review is listed as waiting on its author. \"review\" It is treated like any other review. \"ignore\" It is left off the board. To give your drafts a pane of their own, set mine = \"apart\" and add a pane filtered on is:draft role:author . See Spaces ."}, {"u": "rules.html#nudge", "t": "Rules", "h": "Nudge", "x": "[nudge] after_days = 7 A waiting item that nobody touched for that many days becomes Nudge in To do . 0 , the default, turns it off."}, {"u": "rules.html#ticket-statuses", "t": "Rules", "h": "Ticket statuses", "x": "[tickets] waiting_statuses = [\"blocked\", \"on hold\", \"in review\", \"waiting\"] A ticket in one of these statuses (compared without case) is Blocked , in Waiting . So is a ticket with an \"is blocked by\" link."}, {"u": "urgency.html", "t": "Urgency", "h": "", "x": "A score decides what comes first. It is the sum of three things, each shown on the board. the formula urgency = (100 − rule priority) + waiting + ticket"}, {"u": "urgency.html#the-three-parts", "t": "Urgency", "h": "The three parts", "x": "Part Points From Rule 100 − priority The rule that lists the task. A review to do (priority 10) gives 90; a draft to finish (priority 90) gives 10. Waiting 3 per day, at most 60 The full days since the next step arrived: since the review was requested, since the oldest unanswered reply, since your last word when you wait on someone. Ticket +5, plus the priority A change that names a ticket in its title or branch ( PROJ-12 ) gets 5, plus the points of the ticket's priority when Jira can tell it. A ticket gets the points of its own priority. Ticket priority Points Highest +50 High +30 Medium +10 Low 0 Lowest −10"}, {"u": "urgency.html#an-example", "t": "Urgency", "h": "An example", "x": "i on a task HOW ITS URGENCY ADDS UP rule 80 \"Re-review\" has priority 20 (0 first, 100 last): 100 − 20 waiting +15 5 days × 3 a day ticket +35 tied to PROJ-440, \"high\" (+30), and +5 for naming a ticket urgency = 130 hot: warm ▴ from 100, hot ▲ from 130"}, {"u": "urgency.html#where-the-board-shows-it", "t": "Urgency", "h": "Where the board shows it", "x": "The detail pane sums it up: urgency 130 = rule 80, waiting +15, PROJ-440 (high) +35 . Panes ordered by urgency show the score on every line. i on a task lays it out line by line, with your own weights. ▴ marks a task from 100 points (warm), ▲ from 130 (hot). The filter heat:hot,warm keeps them."}, {"u": "urgency.html#orders", "t": "Urgency", "h": "Orders", "x": "Panes list the most urgent first by default. s changes a pane's order and v reverses it. Order First urgency The highest score; among equals, the one that has waited longest. rule The rules' own order; among equals, the freshest. waiting What has waited longest. updated What moved most recently. created What was opened first."}, {"u": "urgency.html#change-the-weights", "t": "Urgency", "h": "Change the weights", "x": "~/.config/aki/config.toml [urgency] per_day = 3 waiting_cap = 60 linked = 5 highest = 50 high = 30 medium = 10 low = 0 lowest = -10 warm = 100 hot = 130 The rule's part follows the rule's priority: change it under [rules.<name>] . aki rules prints the weights in use."}, {"u": "urgency.html#how-a-change-is-tied-to-a-ticket", "t": "Urgency", "h": "How a change is tied to a ticket", "x": "By a key in its title or branch name, such as PROJ-12 . With a Jira source configured, the key is looked up, even for tickets that are not yours, and its priority counts. Without one, anything shaped like a key counts as a ticket and gets the 5 points."}, {"u": "spaces.html", "t": "Spaces and panes", "h": "", "x": "A space keeps part of the board. Its panes are filtered, grouped and sorted views of it, tiled in a layout."}, {"u": "spaces.html#how-spaces-are-made", "t": "Spaces and panes", "h": "How spaces are made", "x": "On a first run aki makes All , plus one space per source when there are several. From then on spaces are what you make them: every change in the board is saved at once to ~/.config/aki/spaces.toml , which you can also edit by hand. A space has: a scope : a filter saying what belongs to it at all; a layout : how its panes are tiled; one or more panes , each with its own filter, grouping and order."}, {"u": "spaces.html#see-what-a-space-holds", "t": "Spaces and panes", "h": "See what a space holds", "x": "I in the board explains the shown space: its scope, its layout, its panes, and the repositories and projects it holds right now with their counts. aki spaces output 2 Work scope source:gitlab,jira layout master pane 1 To do · filter: is:todo · group: repo · sort: waiting ↓ pane 2 Waiting · filter: is:waiting · group: repo · sort: urgency ↓ holds gitlab · acme/api (7 to do, 2 waiting) gitlab · acme/web (2 to do, 3 waiting)"}, {"u": "spaces.html#work-on-spaces", "t": "Spaces and panes", "h": "Work on spaces", "x": "Key Does 1 - 9 , , . Show a space, or click it in the top bar. N New space. S Its scope. source:github keeps one source, repo:web one repository, -repo:legacy leaves one out. R X Rename it, remove it. t Its layout: columns → rows → master → grid. < > Move it among the others."}, {"u": "spaces.html#work-on-panes", "t": "Spaces and panes", "h": "Work on panes", "x": "Key Does / Filter the pane, applied as you type. b Its side: to do → waiting → both. g Its grouping: none → repo → kind → source → person → role. s v Its order , and the reverse. n x New pane beside this one, with the same view; close it. Shift + ← → Move it among the others. m then 1 - 9 Send it to another space. e Name it. z d Zoom it; show or hide the detail pane."}, {"u": "spaces.html#layouts", "t": "Spaces and panes", "h": "Layouts", "x": "Layout Tiles columns Side by side. rows One above the other. master The first pane large on the left, the others stacked on the right. grid As square a grid as the count allows."}, {"u": "spaces.html#the-file", "t": "Spaces and panes", "h": "The file", "x": "~/.config/aki/spaces.toml [[spaces]] name = \"Work\" scope = \"source:gitlab,jira\" layout = \"master\" [[spaces.panes]] filter = \"is:todo\" group = \"repo\" sort = \"waiting\" [[spaces.panes]] filter = \"is:waiting\" group = \"repo\" sort = \"urgency\" [[spaces.panes]] title = \"My drafts\" filter = \"is:draft role:author\" group = \"repo\" sort = \"urgency\" Key Values scope , filter A filter . Empty: everything. layout columns , rows , master , grid group none , repo , kind , source , person , role sort urgency , rule , waiting , updated , created ; reverse = true flips it title The pane's name. Without it, the pane is named after its filter."}, {"u": "spaces.html#a-pane-for-your-drafts", "t": "Spaces and panes", "h": "A pane for your drafts", "x": "To work on your drafts in their own pane and keep them out of To do : ~/.config/aki/config.toml [drafts] mine = \"apart\" Then, in the board: n for a new pane, type is:draft role:author , Enter , and e to name it. Drafts kept apart show only in panes that ask for is:draft ; the top bar says how many there are."}, {"u": "spaces.html#start-over", "t": "Spaces and panes", "h": "Start over", "x": "aki spaces reset This writes the starting spaces again from your sources. The previous file is kept beside it as spaces.toml.bak ."}, {"u": "filters.html", "t": "Filters", "h": "", "x": "A filter is a short query. It is used for a pane's filter, a space's scope, and on the command line. an example is:todo source:gitlab repo:web,api -is:draft by:alex export Terms are separated by spaces and must all hold. key:a,b holds when any value does. A leading - negates a term. A bare word is searched in the reference, the title, the repository and the person."}, {"u": "filters.html#terms", "t": "Filters", "h": "Terms", "x": "Term Keeps is:todo , is:waiting One side of the board. is:draft Draft changes. The only way to see drafts kept apart . is:snoozed What you set aside , which nothing else shows. source:gitlab,jira Items from any of these sources, by the name you gave them. repo:web Repositories or projects whose path contains it. kind:review Tasks listed for a rule whose name contains it, looking at every reason. aki rules names the rules. top:draft The same, looking only at the most pressing reason. role:author author , reviewer , assignee , participant . by:alex The person on the other side. heat:hot,warm Tasks marked hot or warm; calm for the others. ticket:PROJ Changes that name a ticket whose key contains it. ticket:any : any ticket. priority:high,highest Tickets of that priority, and the changes that name one. agent:blocked Tasks whose agent is working , blocked , done , idle or open . agent:any : has one. export A word in the reference, title, repository or person. -term Everything the term does not keep."}, {"u": "filters.html#where-filters-are-used", "t": "Filters", "h": "Where filters are used", "x": "Place How A pane / in the board. The pane narrows as you type; Esc puts the previous filter back. A space's scope S in the board. The command line aki list --filter \"repo:web kind:review\" The file scope and filter in spaces.toml . An assistant The filter argument of list_tasks ."}, {"u": "filters.html#recipes", "t": "Filters", "h": "Recipes", "x": "To see Filter Reviews and re-reviews to do is:todo kind:review Everything about one repository repo:api What cannot wait is:todo heat:hot Your drafts is:draft role:author Agents that wait for you agent:blocked Work tied to high-priority tickets priority:high,highest What you wait on from one person is:waiting by:alex A filter that does not parse is refused with the reason: an unknown key, or a value the key does not take."}, {"u": "keys.html", "t": "Keys", "h": "", "x": "Every key of the board. ? shows them in the board itself."}, {"u": "keys.html#move", "t": "Keys", "h": "Move", "x": "Key Does ↑ ↓ , j k The task, within the pane. PgUp PgDn , Home End Ten tasks; the first, the last. ← → , h l , Tab The pane. 1 - 9 , , . The space. The mouse works too: click a space, a pane or a task; scroll a pane."}, {"u": "keys.html#a-task", "t": "Keys", "h": "A task", "x": "Key Does Enter , o Open it in the browser, on the thread itself when there is one. i Explain it: why it is listed, how its urgency adds up, what every mark on a line means. a Open your coding agent on it, briefed, in its clone. p Set it aside : t tomorrow, w a week, 1 - 9 days, m until it moves. On a task already aside, bring it back."}, {"u": "keys.html#the-pane", "t": "Keys", "h": "The pane", "x": "Key Does / Filter it, applied as you type. b Its side: to do → waiting → both. g Its grouping: none → repo → kind → source → person → role. s v Its order: urgency → rule → waiting → updated → created; reverse it. n x New pane beside this one; close it. Shift + ← → , H L Move it among the others. m then 1 - 9 Send it to another space. e Name it. z Zoom it; Esc leaves. d Show or hide the detail pane."}, {"u": "keys.html#the-space", "t": "Keys", "h": "The space", "x": "Key Does I Explain it: how it is made, its panes, the repositories it holds. t Its layout: columns → rows → master → grid. N R X New space; rename; remove (asks first). S Its scope: what belongs to it at all. < > Move it among the others."}, {"u": "keys.html#the-board", "t": "Keys", "h": "The board", "x": "Key Does r Refresh now. ? Every key. q , Ctrl + C Quit."}, {"u": "agents.html", "t": "Agents", "h": "", "x": "One key hands a task to your coding agent: in the right place, in the repository's clone, already told what there is to do. a on a task, or from a shell: aki agent web!916 The reference is what the board shows: web!916 , notes#12 , PROJ-7 , a ticket key the change names, or its URL. --dry-run prints where it would open and the brief, without opening anything."}, {"u": "agents.html#the-brief", "t": "Agents", "h": "The brief", "x": "The agent's first message is written from the task: where the work is, why it is listed, and what each reason asks for, most pressing first. the brief of a re-review This comes from my board of things to do. Typed errors for the key store https://gitlab.example/acme/api/-/merge_requests/889 api!889 on gitlab. I am a reviewer; the author is @ana. Ticket: PROJ-440 (high). What there is to do, most pressing first: 1. Re-review: the author replied, new commits. I already reviewed it. Look at what changed since: the commits pushed after my review and the answers to my comments. Tell me whether each of my points was addressed. If they all were and nothing new is wrong, say it is ready to approve. Start here: https://gitlab.example/acme/api/-/merge_requests/889#note_7 2. Resolve threads: 2 answered threads to check and resolve. … Start by reading it where it lives, with the forge's or the tracker's own tools. Then tell me what you found and what you propose. Do not post, approve, merge or push anything before I say so. Every rule has its own request: a review asks for a review, a red pipeline asks to be fixed, a branch behind its target asks for a rebase. instructions adds your own closing words to every brief."}, {"u": "agents.html#set-it-up", "t": "Agents", "h": "Set it up", "x": "~/.config/aki/config.toml [agent] command = \"claude {prompt}\" instructions = \"Answer in French.\" workspace = \"{repo}\" tab = \"{ticket} {ref}\" focus = true Key Meaning command The agent's command. {prompt} is where the brief goes, as one argument; without it the brief is the last argument. A list works too: [\"codex\", \"--full-auto\", \"{prompt}\"] . instructions Added at the end of every brief. workspace , tab The names of where the agent opens. See Names . focus Whether opening an agent takes you to it."}, {"u": "agents.html#where-it-opens", "t": "Agents", "h": "Where it opens", "x": "launcher chooses. \"auto\" , the default, takes Herdr when aki runs inside it, else the terminal aki runs in, else a Claude conversation. [agent] launcher = \"herdr\" One workspace per repository, one tab per piece of work, named from your templates and created when missing. A workspace or a tab is reused only when it bears exactly that name. A tab that is already open is never doubled: an agent runs in it: the new brief is pasted into its prompt and sent; the agent is gone: it is started again in that tab, on the brief; the tab runs something else: nothing is typed, and aki says so. herdr_session = \"work\" opens agents in a named Herdr session instead of the current one. [agent] launcher = \"terminal\" A new window or tab of tmux, Ghostty, WezTerm, kitty, iTerm or Terminal, whichever aki runs in. For another terminal, give your own command: [agent] terminal = [\"alacritty\", \"--title\", \"{title}\", \"-e\", \"{command}\"] {command} is what to run, {title} its name, {directory} where it starts. A plain terminal cannot tell whether a tab is already open, nor what the agent is doing. [agent] launcher = \"claude\" chat_url = \"https://claude.ai/new?q={prompt}\" No terminal: a new Claude conversation opens with the brief as its first message. For the desktop app, try chat_url = \"claude://claude.ai/new?q={prompt}\" . This is what an assistant uses when asked to start on a task."}, {"u": "agents.html#names", "t": "Agents", "h": "Names", "x": "The names come from the task, never from what you already have open. Placeholder Value {repo} The repository's own name: web . {path} Its full path: acme/platform/web . {ref} The reference: !916 , #12 , PROJ-7 . {short} Both: web!916 . {ticket} The first ticket the change names; empty when there is none. {kind} The rule that lists the task: review_requested . {source} Where it comes from: gitlab ."}, {"u": "agents.html#the-clone", "t": "Agents", "h": "The clone", "x": "The agent starts in the repository's local clone, found by its git remote under the folders where you keep your code. Without your word, aki looks in ~/code , ~/src , ~/dev , ~/projects , ~/work , ~/repos , ~/git , ~/Developer and ~/Desktop . [agent] roots = [\"~/code\"] [agent.repos] \"group/project\" = \"~/elsewhere/project\" Without a clone the agent still opens, and the brief carries the link. The agent is started by your own login shell, so it finds the same PATH as at your prompt."}, {"u": "agents.html#what-the-agent-is-doing", "t": "Agents", "h": "What the agent is doing", "x": "Once an agent is open on a task, the board shows its state beside the task, read from the launcher every two seconds. Mark State Filter ◐ Working. agent:working ? Waiting for you. agent:blocked ✓ Done, not looked at yet. agent:done · Idle. agent:idle ○ Its terminal is open; what runs in it is not known. agent:open Only Herdr reports states. A pane filtered on agent:blocked gathers the agents that wait for you."}, {"u": "assistants.html", "t": "Assistants", "h": "", "x": "aki serves the board to an assistant over the Model Context Protocol, for whoever would rather ask than open a terminal. Once plugged in, the assistant can be asked: what waits on me, why is this one first, set that one aside until Monday, start on the review of web!916 ."}, {"u": "assistants.html#plug-it-in", "t": "Assistants", "h": "Plug it in", "x": "aki mcp setup This prints the block below with the full path of your aki . Settings › Developer › Edit Config, add this to claude_desktop_config.json , and restart the app: { \"mcpServers\": { \"aki\": { \"command\": \"/Users/you/.cargo/bin/aki\", \"args\": [\"mcp\"] } } } claude mcp add aki -- aki mcp Any MCP client that starts a server on standard input and output: the command is aki mcp . aki must be installed and its sources signed in on the same machine. An app started outside a shell passes a short PATH ; aki adds /opt/homebrew/bin , /usr/local/bin , ~/.local/bin and ~/.cargo/bin so that glab and gh are found."}, {"u": "assistants.html#tools", "t": "Assistants", "h": "Tools", "x": "Tool Does Arguments list_tasks The board, most urgent first. Every task says why it is listed and how its score is made. side , space , filter , sort , limit get_task One task in full: its reasons, its urgency line by line, its links, and the brief of what is expected. reference list_spaces Your spaces, their panes, the repositories they hold. explain_rules Every rule as configured, and how urgency is computed. set_aside Hide a task for a number of days, or until it moves. reference , days bring_back Put a task that was set aside back on the board. reference start_agent Open your agent on a task, through the launcher you chose. reference A reference is what the board shows: web!916 , notes#12 , PROJ-7 , a ticket key, or the URL. filter takes the same queries as a pane."}, {"u": "assistants.html#what-it-may-do", "t": "Assistants", "h": "What it may do", "x": "Reading the board is always allowed. The rest is yours to say: ~/.config/aki/config.toml [mcp] enabled = true set_aside = true start_agent = true Key When false enabled aki mcp refuses to start. set_aside set_aside and bring_back are neither offered nor done. start_agent start_agent is neither offered nor done. No tool approves, merges, comments or pushes: aki has no such action."}, {"u": "assistants.html#starting-work-from-a-conversation", "t": "Assistants", "h": "Starting work from a conversation", "x": "Without a terminal, start_agent opens a new Claude conversation on the task's brief: [agent] launcher = \"claude\" With launcher = \"auto\" , this is also what happens when aki finds neither Herdr nor a terminal. To work on the task in the conversation at hand instead, ask for the task: get_task returns the same brief."}, {"u": "set-aside.html", "t": "Set aside, be told", "h": "", "x": "Hide a task until it matters again, and hear about what becomes yours."}, {"u": "set-aside.html#set-a-task-aside", "t": "Set aside, be told", "h": "Set a task aside", "x": "p on a task, then for how long: Key Until t Tomorrow. w In a week. 1 - 9 In that many days. m Something happens on it: a comment, a push, a status change. The task leaves the panes, the counts and the notifications. It is still true; it comes back by itself. The top bar says how many tasks are aside."}, {"u": "set-aside.html#see-them-bring-one-back", "t": "Set aside, be told", "h": "See them, bring one back", "x": "A pane filtered on is:snoozed lists what is aside. p on a task there brings it back. aki list --filter is:snoozed What you set aside is kept in ~/.local/state/aki/snoozed.json ."}, {"u": "set-aside.html#notifications", "t": "Set aside, be told", "h": "Notifications", "x": "While the board is open, a task that starts asking something of you is announced: a desktop notification says what, once per refresh. A task that comes back from being set aside is not announced, nor is a source coming back after a failure. ~/.config/aki/config.toml notifications = true"}, {"u": "set-aside.html#sounds", "t": "Set aside, be told", "h": "Sounds", "x": "Something new to do also rings, once per refresh, with the sound of the most pressing new task. [sounds] enabled = true new_task = \"Glass\" [sounds.rules] review_requested = \"Ping\" draft_to_finish = \"none\" Key Value new_task A system sound by name, or a file: \"~/sounds/ding.wav\" . The default is Glass on macOS and message-new-instant elsewhere. [sounds.rules] A sound of its own for a rule . \"none\" keeps it quiet. aki sounds aki sounds Glass The first lists the sounds that can be named; the second plays one."}, {"u": "configuration.html", "t": "Configuration", "h": "", "x": "One TOML file. Every setting has a default; write only what you change. aki config init This writes ~/.config/aki/config.toml with every setting at its default and a comment on each. aki config path prints where the file is. Unknown keys and names are errors."}, {"u": "configuration.html#files", "t": "Configuration", "h": "Files", "x": "File Holds ~/.config/aki/config.toml The settings on this page. $AKI_CONFIG names another file; $XDG_CONFIG_HOME is honored. ~/.config/aki/spaces.toml Your spaces , rewritten when you rearrange the board. ~/.cache/aki/cache.db What was read from the sources (SQLite). $XDG_CACHE_HOME is honored. ~/.local/state/aki/snoozed.json What you set aside. $XDG_STATE_HOME is honored."}, {"u": "configuration.html#general", "t": "Configuration", "h": "General", "x": "refresh_seconds = 30 notifications = true cache_seconds = 60 Key Meaning refresh_seconds How often the board looks again. Minimum 5. notifications A desktop notification when something new becomes yours. cache_seconds aki list reuses a reading younger than this. 0 : always ask."}, {"u": "configuration.html#sources", "t": "Configuration", "h": "Sources", "x": "[[sources]] kind = \"gitlab\" [[sources]] kind = \"github\" [[sources]] kind = \"jira\" site = \"https://your-company.atlassian.net\" email = \"you@your-company.com\" token_env = \"JIRA_API_TOKEN\" Every key is on Sources ."}, {"u": "configuration.html#rules", "t": "Configuration", "h": "Rules", "x": "[threads] who_resolves = \"reviewer\" ignore_bots = true [drafts] mine = \"todo\" others = \"wait\" [re_review] triggers = [\"author_replied\", \"new_commits\", \"re_requested\", \"approval_reset\"] after_approval = false [tickets] waiting_statuses = [\"blocked\", \"on hold\", \"in review\", \"waiting\"] [nudge] after_days = 0 [rules.checks_running] bucket = \"todo\" priority = 45 Every key is on Rules ."}, {"u": "configuration.html#urgency", "t": "Configuration", "h": "Urgency", "x": "[urgency] per_day = 3 waiting_cap = 60 linked = 5 highest = 50 high = 30 medium = 10 low = 0 lowest = -10 warm = 100 hot = 130 Every key is on Urgency ."}, {"u": "configuration.html#agent", "t": "Configuration", "h": "Agent", "x": "[agent] command = \"claude {prompt}\" instructions = \"\" launcher = \"auto\" chat_url = \"https://claude.ai/new?q={prompt}\" workspace = \"{repo}\" tab = \"{ticket} {ref}\" focus = true # terminal = [\"alacritty\", \"--title\", \"{title}\", \"-e\", \"{command}\"] # herdr_session = \"work\" # roots = [\"~/code\"] # [agent.repos] # \"group/project\" = \"~/elsewhere/project\" Every key is on Agents ."}, {"u": "configuration.html#sounds", "t": "Configuration", "h": "Sounds", "x": "[sounds] enabled = true # new_task = \"Glass\" # [sounds.rules] # review_requested = \"Ping\" Every key is on Set aside, be told ."}, {"u": "configuration.html#assistants", "t": "Configuration", "h": "Assistants", "x": "[mcp] enabled = true set_aside = true start_agent = true Every key is on Assistants ."}, {"u": "sources.html", "t": "Sources", "h": "", "x": "Where aki reads from: GitLab, GitHub and Jira Cloud."}, {"u": "sources.html#without-configuration", "t": "Sources", "h": "Without configuration", "x": "aki uses gitlab.com when glab is installed and github.com when gh is, with their own logins. Nothing to write. aki doctor It checks every source and prints who you are signed in as."}, {"u": "sources.html#declare-your-sources", "t": "Sources", "h": "Declare your sources", "x": "Declaring [[sources]] replaces the detection: list every source you want."}, {"u": "sources.html#gitlab", "t": "Sources", "h": "GitLab", "x": "[[sources]] kind = \"gitlab\" host = \"gitlab.acme.io\" host defaults to gitlab.com . The token comes from $GITLAB_TOKEN when set, else from glab config get token . When the token is refused, aki has glab renew it and tries again."}, {"u": "sources.html#github", "t": "Sources", "h": "GitHub", "x": "[[sources]] kind = \"github\" host defaults to github.com . The token comes from $GITHUB_TOKEN when set, else from gh auth token ."}, {"u": "sources.html#jira", "t": "Sources", "h": "Jira", "x": "[[sources]] kind = \"jira\" site = \"https://your-company.atlassian.net\" email = \"you@your-company.com\" token_env = \"JIRA_API_TOKEN\" Jira Cloud, with an API token . jql changes which tickets are yours; the default is: jql = \"assignee = currentUser() AND statusCategory != Done ORDER BY updated DESC\""}, {"u": "sources.html#keys", "t": "Sources", "h": "Keys", "x": "Key Meaning kind gitlab , github or jira . name Shown on the board and used by source: filters. Defaults to the kind. Two sources of the same kind need different names. host GitLab and GitHub: the instance. site , email , jql Jira: the site, your account, the query. token_env An environment variable holding the token. token_command A command that prints the token, for a keychain or a password manager. token_renew_command A command run when the token is refused, before trying again. a token from the macOS keychain token_command = \"security find-generic-password -s aki-jira -w\" Tokens are read from the environment or a command each time. aki never stores one."}, {"u": "sources.html#what-is-read", "t": "Sources", "h": "What is read", "x": "Source Items GitLab Open merge requests you wrote, review or are assigned to, with their threads, approvals, pipeline and branch state; issues assigned to you. GitHub Open pull requests you are involved in (author, assignee, commenter, mentioned), are asked to review or have reviewed, with their review threads, reviews and checks; issues assigned to you. Jira The tickets your query returns, with status, priority, blocking links and mentions; and the priority of tickets your changes name."}, {"u": "sources.html#the-cache", "t": "Sources", "h": "The cache", "x": "Everything read is kept in one SQLite file, ~/.cache/aki/cache.db . The board opens at once on what was known last time, then refreshes. A source that is down still shows what it said last, marked as such. Discussions are read again only when the item moved; a ticket looked up for its priority is trusted for half an hour. A refresh is a handful of light requests. It holds who spoke when and where. It holds neither what was said nor any token. aki cache path aki cache clear"}, {"u": "sources.html#known-limits", "t": "Sources", "h": "Known limits", "x": "GitLab: merge requests where you only commented, without being author, assignee or reviewer, are not listed. GitLab tells its history in English system notes; pushes and re-requests are read from those. GitHub says a branch is behind its target only where the branch must be up to date to merge. Jira: Cloud only. \"Flagged\" is not read; use waiting_statuses or \"is blocked by\" links."}, {"u": "cli.html", "t": "Command line", "h": "", "x": "Every command. aki alone opens the board in a terminal, and prints the list when piped."}, {"u": "cli.html#commands", "t": "Command line", "h": "Commands", "x": "Command Does aki The live board in a terminal; the list when piped. aki watch The live board. aki list Print the board once. See below . aki agent REF Open your agent on a task. --dry-run only says where, and prints the brief. aki spaces Your spaces : how each is made, what it holds. aki spaces reset Start them over from your sources; the old file is kept as spaces.toml.bak . aki mcp Serve the board to an assistant . aki mcp setup What to paste where to plug it in. aki rules Every rule and weight as configured. aki doctor Check the connection to every source. aki sounds [NAME] List the sounds that can be named, or play one. aki cache path , clear Where the cache is; empty it. aki config path , init Where the configuration is; write one with the defaults. aki help , version"}, {"u": "cli.html#aki-list", "t": "Command line", "h": "aki list", "x": "aki list --todo --space Work --filter \"repo:web -is:draft\" --sort waiting Option Meaning --todo , --waiting Only one side. --space NAME Only what belongs to one of your spaces. --filter QUERY A filter . --sort ORDER urgency (default), rule , waiting , updated , created . --reverse The opposite order. --fresh Ask the sources even if a recent reading is cached. --json Machine-readable. --count One line."}, {"u": "cli.html#in-a-prompt-or-a-status-bar", "t": "Command line", "h": "In a prompt or a status bar", "x": "aki list --count output 11 to do · 13 waiting · 3 set aside · 19 drafts apart A reading younger than cache_seconds (60 by default) is reused, so the command returns at once when called often."}, {"u": "cli.html#json", "t": "Command line", "h": "JSON", "x": "aki list --json --todo one task, shortened { \"id\": \"gitlab:acme/api!889\", \"source\": \"gitlab\", \"container\": \"acme/api\", \"reference\": \"!889\", \"title\": \"Typed errors for the key store\", \"url\": \"https://gitlab.example/acme/api/-/merge_requests/889\", \"role\": \"reviewer\", \"counterpart\": \"ana\", \"bucket\": \"todo\", \"waiting_since\": 1794000000, \"urgency\": { \"score\": 130, \"rule\": 80, \"waiting\": 15, \"ticket\": 35, \"heat\": \"hot\" }, \"draft\": false, \"tickets\": [{ \"key\": \"PROJ-440\", \"priority\": \"high\" }], \"reasons\": [ { \"kind\": \"re_review\", \"bucket\": \"todo\", \"priority\": 20, \"why\": \"the author replied, new commits\" } ] } The document has todo and waiting lists, the sources that answered, and the failures of those that did not. Times are seconds since 1970."}, {"u": "cli.html#exit-status", "t": "Command line", "h": "Exit status", "x": "Status Meaning 0 Done. aki list succeeds as long as something could be shown, even from the cache. 1 aki list : no source could be read and nothing was remembered. aki doctor : a source failed. 2 A command or the configuration could not be understood."}, {"u": "faq.html", "t": "FAQ", "h": "", "x": "Short answers."}, {"u": "faq.html#does-aki-change-anything-on-gitlab-github-or-jira", "t": "FAQ", "h": "Does aki change anything on GitLab, GitHub or Jira?", "x": "No. It only reads. It has no action that approves, merges, comments, transitions or pushes. Enter opens the page in your browser; you act there."}, {"u": "faq.html#where-does-my-data-go", "t": "FAQ", "h": "Where does my data go?", "x": "Nowhere but your machine. aki talks to your own sources with your own tokens, and keeps a local cache of who spoke when. It has no server and no account. The cache holds neither the text of comments nor any token."}, {"u": "faq.html#why-does-it-poll-instead-of-receiving-events", "t": "FAQ", "h": "Why does it poll instead of receiving events?", "x": "None of the three services pushes events to a personal client. aki asks every 30 seconds and keeps it cheap: a few light requests, and discussions read again only when an item moved."}, {"u": "faq.html#a-task-is-missing-why", "t": "FAQ", "h": "A task is missing. Why?", "x": "It asks nothing of you and you wait on nothing: an approved change of someone else's, for example. It is set aside: look at a pane filtered on is:snoozed . It is a draft of yours kept apart or ignored: see Drafts . Its rule is turned off: aki rules shows which are on. The space's scope or the pane's filter leaves it out: I shows both. On GitLab, you only commented on it: see Known limits ."}, {"u": "faq.html#why-is-this-task-above-that-one", "t": "FAQ", "h": "Why is this task above that one?", "x": "i on each: the window lays the urgency out line by line. If the pane is not ordered by urgency, its title says by what."}, {"u": "faq.html#how-do-i-keep-my-drafts-out-of-to-do", "t": "FAQ", "h": "How do I keep my drafts out of \"To do\"?", "x": "mine = \"apart\" under [drafts] , and a pane filtered on is:draft role:author . See A pane for your drafts ."}, {"u": "faq.html#can-i-use-two-accounts-of-the-same-service", "t": "FAQ", "h": "Can I use two accounts of the same service?", "x": "Yes: declare two sources of that kind with different name , host or token. See Sources ."}, {"u": "faq.html#does-it-work-with-a-self-hosted-gitlab-or-github-enterprise", "t": "FAQ", "h": "Does it work with a self-hosted GitLab or GitHub Enterprise?", "x": "Set host on the source. Jira is Cloud only."}, {"u": "faq.html#which-agent-does-a-open", "t": "FAQ", "h": "Which agent does a open?", "x": "Claude Code by default. Any command works: set command under [agent] . See Agents ."}, {"u": "faq.html#can-i-use-it-without-a-terminal", "t": "FAQ", "h": "Can I use it without a terminal?", "x": "Yes, through an assistant: aki mcp serves the board to Claude Desktop or any MCP client. See Assistants . aki itself still has to be installed on the machine."}, {"u": "faq.html#does-it-run-on-windows", "t": "FAQ", "h": "Does it run on Windows?", "x": "It is developed and used on macOS. The Linux paths (notifications, sounds, opening links) are written but have not been tested yet. It has not been run on Windows."}, {"u": "faq.html#what-does-the-name-mean", "t": "FAQ", "h": "What does the name mean?", "x": "À qui ? is French for \"whose turn?\"."}];
